<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shangqing</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shangqing school</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shangqing ('Highest Clarity') is a school of Daoism based on revelations received in the 360s by Yang Xi, who wrote down scriptures dictated, he said, by perfected immortals, for an aristocratic family near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a>. Emphasising meditation, visualisation and individual spiritual ascent, it appealed to the southern aristocracy. Tao Hongjing edited its texts around 500 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-mao">Mount Mao</a>, which became its centre, and it was a leading form of Daoism under the Tang.</p></div>
